the intervals as a comma-separated list. Use interval notation: for example, 
(-17,20) is the interval <m>-17 \lt  x \lt  20</m>, and (-inf, 40) is the interval
<m>x\lt 40</m>.</p>
<p>Interval(s) where <m>f</m> is increasing:  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Interval(s) where <m>f</m> is decreasing:  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>Does <m>f</m> have a global maximum? If so, enter its value. If not, enter DNE.</p>
<p>Global maximum = <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>Determine the following limits.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\lim_{x\rightarrow \infty}} f(x) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\lim_{x\rightarrow -\infty}} f(x) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
