</li>
<li>
<p>The term <m>(x+1)^2</m> is positive for all values of <m>x</m>, so <m>\displaystyle{\frac{3}{1+(x+1)^2}}</m> is always positive and <m>f(x)&gt;2</m> for all values of <m>x</m>.</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>Does <m>f</m> have a global minimum? If so, enter its value. If not, enter DNE.</p>
